title: Genesis 17 – The Covenant of Circumcision
description: A study in Genesis 17: Abram becomes Abraham, circumcision given as the token of the covenant, a picture of the circumcision of the heart, and Isaac promised.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-17-circumcision.html

=== Introduction
--- The Covenant of Circumcision [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 17
sub: Abram becomes Abraham, and the token of the covenant.
refs: Genesis 17:1-5; Genesis 17:10-11
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== A new name
--- Thy name shall be Abraham
scripture: Genesis 17:1-5 | mark: thy name shall be Abraham; a father of many nations have I made thee
stat: 99 | Abraham’s age
stat: 24 | years since he called on the name of the {Lord}
p: Now Abram becomes Abraham, decades after his salvation by calling upon the name of the {Lord}, and is given the physical sign of the covenant, circumcision of the flesh. [[Genesis 12:4]] [[Genesis 12:8]]

--- The names
panel: Abram | “Exalted father.”
panel: Abraham | “Because I give you to be father of many nations.”
panel: Sarai and Sarah | Both mean “princess,” a mighty woman. Sarai is the possessive form: Abram called her “my princess.” As Sarah, she is *the* princess, the queen of the multitudes of nations, essentially. [[Genesis 17:15-16]]
center: We see name changes as something God does, whether Jesus renaming the apostles or Saul becoming Paul. Neither incidental nor coincidental. Everything is done for a purpose. [[John 1:42]] [[Acts 13:9]]

=== The token of the covenant
--- Every man child
scripture: Genesis 17:9-14 | mark: it shall be a token of the covenant betwixt me and you
p: The descendants of Abraham kept circumcision as an ordinance, to remember their covenant with God that brought about Christ Jesus in the flesh, to preserve the seed even as strangers and bondsmen were added to the nation, in case any forgot God’s promise.

--- After he was saved
scripture: Romans 4:9-11 | mark: Not in circumcision, but in uncircumcision; a seal of the righteousness of the faith which he had yet being uncircumcised
center: Abraham believed God and was counted righteous before he was circumcised. The sign followed the faith. [[Genesis 15:6]]

--- The circumcision of the heart
lead: This physical act of obedience was a picture of the sealing of a soul by the Holy Spirit to come. The circumcision of the heart.
scripture: Romans 2:28-29 | mark: circumcision is that of the heart, in the spirit
scripture: Colossians 2:11 | mark: the circumcision made without hands
p: The circumcision of the heart, which is found in believers, is to us who are saved a reminder of our salvation and belonging to the body of Christ. [[Ephesians 1:13]]

=== Isaac promised
--- Abraham laughed
scripture: Genesis 17:15-17 | mark: laughed
p: Despite his deep faith and willingness to obey, Abraham was human, second-guessing the power of God and His faithfulness to keep His promises. God assures Abraham that within the year Sarah will bear a son, and he shall name him Isaac. [[Genesis 17:19]] [[Genesis 17:21]]

--- O that Ishmael might live
scripture: Genesis 17:18-21 | mark: But my covenant will I establish with Isaac
p: To satisfy the prayer for Ishmael from Abraham, God says He will bless the elder son, of the bondwoman. But the covenant is with the younger, and, like Esau and Jacob, *the elder shall serve the younger*. [[Genesis 25:23]] [[lesson:genesis-16-hagar-and-ishmael|Genesis 16]]

=== The selfsame day
--- In the selfsame day
scripture: Genesis 17:23-27 | mark: in the selfsame day; Ishmael his son was thirteen years old
p: Another lesson from this is how quickly Abraham obeys the {Lord} in something that seems crazy, I’m sure. Not only does he obey, but he makes all the men of his household obey, including his 13 year old son.

--- Pray to be a father like Abraham
lead: Parents today say things like, “It’s so hard to get my teenager to not watch inappropriate material, or to dress modestly, or to go to church.”
p: Here Abraham is telling his 13 year old son that he’s got to cut off his foreskin. And not only the 13 year old son, but all the men of his house, including servants, herdsmen and slaves.
big: Genesis 18:19 | mark: he will command his children and his household after him
center: Pray to be a father like Abraham.

=== Close
--- The circumcision made without hands [title]
overline: Genesis 17
point: A new name | A father of many nations, and Sarah the princess.
point: The token followed the faith | Abraham was saved decades before he was circumcised.
point: The circumcision of the heart | In the spirit, made without hands, by Christ.
point: The selfsame day | Abraham obeyed at once, and led his house to obey.

